# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fleets Dispatcher — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
# In IBM Code Engine, set these as environment variables / a secret on the application.
# For Docker:  docker run --env-file .env ...   (do not wrap values in quotes)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Authentication ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# PRIMARY (Code Engine deployment) — Trusted Profile
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   The app uses a trusted profile for ALL IBM Cloud interactions — Code Engine API
#   and COS — when deployed to Code Engine. No API key, no HMAC credentials, nothing
#   to rotate. The single IAM bearer token obtained from the trusted profile is shared
#   for both services.
#
#   Setup:
#     1. Create an IAM trusted profile that trusts this Code Engine application as a
#        compute resource. Grant it:
#          - Code Engine: Viewer + Fleet Operator (list projects, list fleets, add tasks)
#          - COS bucket:  Writer (put objects for uploads)
#     2. Enable trusted profiles on the CE application:
#          ibmcloud ce app update --name fleets-dispatcher --trusted-profiles-enabled=true
#     3. Set one of the variables below. Code Engine automatically mounts the compute
#        resource token at the path shown in CR_TOKEN_FILE_PATH.
#
# TRUSTED_PROFILE_ID=Profile-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# TRUSTED_PROFILE_NAME=my-dispatcher-profile
#
# Note: TRUSTED_PROFILE_ID takes precedence over TRUSTED_PROFILE_NAME when both are set.
# Note: With a trusted profile active, /api/presign returns 501 (IAM bearer tokens cannot
#       sign S3 presigned URLs); uploads always stream through /api/upload instead.

# FALLBACK (non-Code-Engine container deployments) — IBM Cloud API key
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Used when NO trusted profile is configured. For local development or running the
#   container outside Code Engine. The key authenticates both CE API calls and the
#   CE-secret lookup that retrieves HMAC credentials for COS.
#
#   Create a key: ibmcloud iam api-key-create dispatcher-key
#   On Code Engine, store it as a secret and inject it:
#     ibmcloud ce secret create --name dispatcher-secrets \
#       --from-literal IBMCLOUD_API_KEY=<your-key>
#     ibmcloud ce app update --name fleets-dispatcher \
#       --env-from-secret dispatcher-secrets
#
# IBMCLOUD_API_KEY=your-ibm-cloud-api-key-here

# ── Advanced trusted-profile options ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Path to the compute resource token file.
# Default: /var/run/secrets/codeengine.cloud.ibm.com/compute-resource-token/token
# Override for local testing only (point at a file containing a real CR token).
# CR_TOKEN_FILE_PATH=/tmp/cr-token

# ── CE region discovery (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────

# Single region injected automatically by Code Engine at runtime.
# When set, only this region is scanned for projects and fleets.
# CE_REGION=us-south

# Comma-separated list of regions for local multi-region testing.
# Ignored when CE_REGION is set.
# CE_REGIONS=us-south,us-east,eu-de,eu-gb,eu-es,jp-tok,jp-osa,au-syd,br-sao,ca-tor

# ── Upload configuration (NEXT_PUBLIC_ = baked in at BUILD time) ──────────────
# Setting these in a running container has no effect. For Docker pass
# --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_...; for local dev put them in .env.local.

# How many files to upload in parallel.
# Default: navigator.hardwareConcurrency (capped at 12). Override if needed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_CONCURRENT_UPLOADS=6

# How many times to retry a failed upload before skipping the file.
# Default: 3. Set to 1 to disable retries.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_UPLOAD_RETRIES=3

# Per-file upload timeout in milliseconds. Default: 600000 (10 minutes).
# Increase for very large files on slow connections.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UPLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS=600000

# ── Presigned URL configuration (server-side) ─────────────────────────────────

# How long (in seconds) a presigned PUT URL remains valid.
# Default: 3600 (1 hour). Increase for large files on slow links (e.g. 21600 = 6 h).
# PRESIGN_EXPIRY_SECONDS=3600

# ── Debug / demo ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to true to run without real IBM Cloud credentials.
# Simulates all API calls; no files are actually uploaded.
# DEMO_MODE=true

# Set to true to enable the API debug panel in production without demo mode.
# ENABLE_DEBUG=true

# Port the server listens on (default: 8080, matches Code Engine's expected port).
# PORT=8080
